    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1116">

                <pb facs="1299" n="1103" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1103"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Italy)/7–2645: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1116<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-27T20:00:00-04:00">July 27, 1945—8 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1256. Appointment of Douglas as Chief Commissioner (urtel 2108, July 26<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d1116-f1"/> and previous) depends upon outcome of Potsdam
                    discussions. Douglas does not desire to proceed to Italy for consultation prior
                    to definite appointment about September 1, as suggested by SACMed, and has
                    requested that his nomination be withdrawn. McCloy is now discussing situation
                    further with British officials, and you will be informed as soon as final
                    decision is reached.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1116-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                        <lb/> J[ohn] D H[ickerson] </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1116-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1116-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed. Cf. <ref target="#d1111">document No. 1111</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1116-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1116-f2-content">
                <p>Douglas’ decision not to accept the proposed appointment was final, but no
                    message to Kirk informing him of this fact has been found.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
